Exiting Chroot Environment and First Boot

1. Clean up temporary source files and build artifacts inside /sources:

`rm -rf /sources/*`

2. Exit the chroot environment back to the host system:

`exit`

3. Unmount pseudo-filesystems and target partitions cleanly from the host:

`umount -vR /mnt/klfs/boot/efi`
`umount -vR /mnt/klfs/dev/pts`
`umount -vR /mnt/klfs/dev`
`umount -vR /mnt/klfs/proc`
`umount -vR /mnt/klfs/sys`
`umount -vR /mnt/klfs`

4. Reboot into your new Kinda Linux From Scratch system:

`reboot`
